WEBVTT

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.190
What the heck? He's not diving at all.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.170
It can't be that he's scared, right?

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.040
He's not used to it yet.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.630
Not the flat platform, or the feel of the concrete.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.970
Or even having an audience.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.440
But look at those muscles.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:27.710
What a jump!

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:30.220
That's so high.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.940
Zero points for the entry, though.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.190
That splash is no good at all.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.360
It's low.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.700
And the water is shallow and tastes like chemicals.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.530
I guess there are always people better than you.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:02.950
What?

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.510
I've never seen such dynamic diving before.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.410
I'll give you that, but...

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.100
But what?

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.430
You won't win with that.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.460
What?

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.280
This isn't the ocean. It's a pool.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.940
<i>I can't decide which one is more amazing.</i>

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.630
Did you see that? That was a standard dive.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.740
What a boring jump.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.500
Anybody could do that.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.730
Why's everything so small here?

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.750
Winning here wouldn't even bring me any satisfaction.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.750
<i>Youichi's diving is perfect.</i>

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:58.260
<i>Okitsu isn't at that level yet,
but he has a dynamic quality Youichi lacks.</i>

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.740
<i>I wonder what I have.</i>

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:16.530
<i>Too slow!</i>

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.060
Why did you stop at one?

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.020
Um, I...

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.410
Speak up.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.920
I thought I was too slow.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.040
Too slow? What was?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.920
When I see the five-meter platform there,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.920
I won't make it unless I've already finished my second flip.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.740
Try it again for me.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.930
Okay.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.200
Did you see the platform this time?

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.200
Yes, that's why I spun around quickly.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.420
See what no one else has ever seen

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.510
I have a proposal for all of you.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.850
There's going to be a large training camp in Beijing this August.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:54.330
It's a two-week training camp that gathers talented teenage divers from all over Asia.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.520
Only three boys and three girls are accepted.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.720
There'll be qualifiers held in Tatsumi to choose those members.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:06.450
The Japan Swimming Federation is planning
to train Olympic athletes from among the six.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.840
When are these qualifiers?

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.040
July 29th.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.150
July?

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.290
Yes.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.290
There's only three and a half months.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:22.730
But if there's any hope of getting you no-names qualified for the Olympics,

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.430
while it may be a little rough, it's our best chance.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.430
Although, you're really going to have to step it up.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.000
What's that mean?

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.230
Sakai.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.180
Yes?

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.440
I want you doing a forward three-and-a-half somersault at the qualifiers.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.440
Huh?!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.940
Three-and-a-half?! There's no way I could—

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.450
But there's only 18 months until the Tokyo Olympics.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.950
While you've made great strides in the last month,

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.210
there are still many more out there better than you.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:01.210
In a competition where kids from all
over Japan are fighting tooth and nail,

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.320
how else are we supposed to showcase Sakai Tomoki's diving?

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.220
Well...

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.510
Three-and-a-half.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:14.590
If you can do a three-and-a-half, something only a handful of junior high students have done before,

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.730
then the judges will take notice.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:20.960
I promise that you'll see it reflected in your scores.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.780
<i>This is a nightmare.</i>

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.150
Sakai.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:54.760
Sakai!

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.770
Yes!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.370
You'll do it, won't you?

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.770
You can do it.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.150
That's what your body is telling me.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:10.730
Building all that muscle has given your rotations more speed.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.660
It's the result of your independent training.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:19.120
It's also given you more time to adjust your entry.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.670
So I know you can do it.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.180
I'll do it.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:33.510
Good.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.250
Get ready to work hard for it.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.090
Okay.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.280
Did you hear that, Okitsu?

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.640
Huh?

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.440
You should be prepared too.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.080
If you don't want to lose to a kid in junior high.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:52.450
That goes for the rest of you too. I hope you haven't forgotten.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:58.690
If one of you isn't chosen to become an Olympic athlete,
then MDC will be shut down.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.960
So this is for MDC, huh?

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:12.650
In other words, you want to send
us to the Olympics for MDC's sake.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:16.120
Or is it for your dead grandfather?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.220
Or is it to protect your own job?

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:34.440
Yes, it's for MDC's sake, but it's also for my grandfather and my own self-interest as well.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:36.870
But so what?

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.370
What do you mean?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.700
Fujitani, you said you wanted to go to the Olympics before.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:43.870
Of course.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.880
For whose sake?

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.750
My own.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:49.990
That's right.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:55.760
All you need to worry about are your own feelings, not mine.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:02.520
If you're the ones going to the Olympics,
then the praise and glory you earn there are all your own.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:04.190
Don't forget that.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.040
Youichi!

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.040
Somebody call an ambulance!

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:28.490
Hurry!

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.450
How do you feel?

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:09.400
Your mother thinks you should be ready to get back to practice soon.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.460
But...

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.460
But what?

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:17.500
I do feel better, but my legs start
shaking when I look at a platform.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:20.840
I don't think I'm ready yet.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:21.810
Okay.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.480
But there won't be much point to practice until you show up.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.480
Everyone is still pretty traumatized by your accident.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.450
They're scared to dive.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:39.490
If you quit diving here,
nobody else will be able to overcome that.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:40.740
So...

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.980
Please, Youichi. Come to practice.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.750
For MDC's sake.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.030
<i>There's a wind blowing.</i>

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:14.270
<i>It's giving MDC a second chance.</i>

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.450
<i>I want to ride this wind.</i>

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.210
<i>I'll ride it.</i>

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.320
<i>If you've got the will, then continue to climb to the top.</i>

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:35.290
<i>There's a view only you can see.</i>

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.850
Too slow. You're tucking way too late.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:50.760
You have to grab your shins as
soon as you enter your rotation.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:51.600
Okay!

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.160
Your judgment is slightly off.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.860
Throw your arms out about half a second sooner.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:05.370
Look up about three more centimeters during your approach.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.390
Okay!

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.630
Listen, there's no point in doing this just to say you've tried.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:14.260
If you're going to do this, you need to succeed.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:15.450
I'm counting on you.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.130
Okay.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:20.830
You seem pretty enthusiastic, Tomo.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:21.680
Yeah.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:24.520
It's really hard, but it's also fun!

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:27.440
Must be nice to have your own personal coach.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.140
What?

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.670
It's not like that.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.140
She's all of our coach.

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:33.890
Let's all do our best.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.240
Sacchin, where's Ryou and Reiji?

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:59.100
They just left.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:12:59.920
No way.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.920
They're probably waiting outside.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.400
Oh, right.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:10.170
Huh?

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:12.310
Ryou! Reiji!

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.070
It's time to go off on your own, kid.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.330
Hey, Chikuwa.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.630
What do you think is going on with Ryou and Reiji?

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:32.580
Are you two still in the lobby?

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:32.580
I just finished practice too

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:32.580
Let's head home together

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:32.580
Did I just miss you guys?

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:32.580
I'll try to catch up with you

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:38.320
Did I say something wrong?

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.200
Hey!

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.200
Thanks.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Miu

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Incoming Call

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Answer

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Decline

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Message

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.200
Hello? What's wrong?

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:51.370
<i>I could ask you the same, Tomo.</i>

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:53.280
Huh? What do you mean?

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.720
<i>You sound a little down.</i>

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:55.970
<i>Did something happen?</i>

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.360
Yeah, a few things.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:01.700
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:04.360
<i>Okay, I'll cheer you up then!</i>

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:05.410
What?

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:09.730
<i>The weather is supposed to be great tomorrow.</i>

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:10.870
Yeah?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.870
<i>I've got a big surprise for you!</i>

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.750
It'll just be a little longer.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:23.170
It's not that I like cooking or anything,

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:26.760
but after ten years of being divorced, it's something you just get good at.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.660
Time to put in the cod.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:38.350
Did you know the character for cod is made by writing the characters for fish and snow?

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.960
I had no idea!

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:45.220
All right, it's almost ready to eat!

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:48.400
Hey, are you even listening?!

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:53.630
God, you talk a lot.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:58.790
I told you, I've been divorced ten years.
Obviously I'm going to start talking to myself.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:03.250
Now I grate some daikon radish over it to make it snow.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.920
And there you have it, snow stew!

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:14.420
This is a special treat, just so you know.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:18.040
It's to commemorate the start of us living together.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:26.750
It's great that Tsugaru has such a nice local specialty like this snow stew.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:30.400
You Tokyo people just decided to name it that.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.910
It's a regular stew for us.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:35.430
Man, why can't you be nicer?

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:39.460
You know, you should talk to the others more during practice.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:42.460
I didn't come here to talk.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:48.230
I mean, that's true, but you don't know anything about diving yet.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:49.970
You could learn something from them.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.470
Like what?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.720
What they're doing is child's play.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.620
Then why did you come to Tokyo?

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:58.470
None of your business.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.040
It's fine.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.340
You can tell me anything. You don't have to hold back.

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:08.480
Then...

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.850
Oh, that's a little unexpected.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:11.740
What is it?

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.840
This ain't the season for stew.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:17.960
Sorry.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:35.220
Come on. Eat up.

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:53.600
God, this is boring.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.700
Ta-da!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.050
What do you think? I made it with my mom.

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:04.540
It looks amazing!

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:08.060
Thanks.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:12.050
It's from the top ten favorite side dish survey I gave you before.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:20.810
There's rolled egg, fried chicken, sausage, spaghetti, Salisbury steak, fried rice, fried noodles, rice balls,

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.670
cream croquette, and French fries.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:27.140
Isn't that a lot of carbs?

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.700
It's not bad if it's just once in a while!

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.320
I guess not.

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:35.460
Mom said that you were a nice boy while we were making it.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.820
That she could tell from looking at your top ten.

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:40.830
Okay then.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.240
I was right!

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:44.410
I knew it.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:45.540
Knew what?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.420
My mom and I had a bet on what you'd pick first.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:53.590
She said the rice balls,
but I knew you'd go for the Salisbury steak.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.030
That so?

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.360
Hey, Miu.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.860
Huh? What is it?

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:17.940
Do you ever feel like you're being fenced in?

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:19.860
Fenced in?

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:20.750
Yeah.

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:28.370
I'm not sure if I can describe it that well, but it feels
like you're being penned inside a really small space.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:34.000
Whenever I think about having to live inside
there for the rest of my life, I get really anxious.

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:36.400
But...

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.380
But?

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:39.320
But then I had a thought.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:42.290
I might be able to break free with diving.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:51.300
My coach told me that if I strive for the top,
I'll reach a view only I can see.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:53.650
And that I had what it took.

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:56.430
That's why I want to escape my pen.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:00.330
I want to leap out of this small and confined world I'm in now.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.580
That's the thought I had.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.070
Sorry.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.460
I know it's probably boring to hear.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.820
It's okay.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:16.170
I think it's great that you view diving like that.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:17.920
Really?

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:19.200
Yeah!

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:24.760
I'm sure you'll be able to overcome
the things that keep most of us back.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:30.440
I think that watching you do that makes us feel like we've overcome something ourselves too.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.440
Thanks.

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:34.000
Don't mention it.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.950
Now, let's eat.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:36.910
Yeah!

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.200
Coming through!

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:52.960
<i>I won't let anything hold me back.</i>

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.830
<i>I'll break out of my tiny pen...</i>

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.700
<i>with this three-and-a-half somersault!</i>

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:15.230
You can make it with those eyes of yours.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:21.740
Damn it!

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:24.390
All right, hurry up and get out.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.690
Man, Youichi is so great.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.220
He's nothing special.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.030
Long time no see, Fujitani Youichi!
